\section{Experience}
\runsubsection{Jump Trading}

\descript{Head of Market Structure | Jan 2025 - Present}
\begin{tightemize}
\item Shape and publicly advocate for Jump's opinions on market structure topics such as exchange design and implementation, product specifications, and regulatory proposals.
\item Regularly interact with exchange C-suite executives, regulators, and governments globally, conveying deeply nuanced technical topics to non-technical audiences.
\item Drive internal initiatives to adapt Jump's trading systems to specific exchange nuance, in conjunction with trading teams, Performance Engineering, and Core Development.
\end{tightemize}

\descript{Lead Quant Developer | Trading Team | Jan 2025 - Present}
\begin{tightemize}
\item Principal engineer for a mid-sized futures trading team, managing a team of experienced engineers.
\item Set the direction for the team's research (python) and execution (C++) platforms.
\item Authored the team's execution stack employing a custom python DSL/compiler atop a low-latency C++/CUDA engine, making it easy for researchers to test new features without sacrificing performance in production.
\item Designed the team's Torch-based research platform with strong reproducibility guarantees and modular components that independently map onto Jump's HPC grid.
\item Designed, implemented, and maintain the firm's most popular grid-compute tooling, allowing researchers to easily fan compute jobs out across a Slurm cluster.  Adoption grew by word-of-mouth to 500+ users firmwide.
\end{tightemize}

\descript{Lead Quant Developer | Central Trading \& Research | July 2019 - Jan 2026}
\begin{tightemize}
\item US lead for "Central Trading \& Research", a "special projects" and central trading team responsible for microstructure research and proprietary feed design.
\item Designed Jump's exchange-feed normalizations used in MF/LF contexts, prioritizing information content and ease-of-use over lowest-latency.
\item Pioneered a new data warehouse paradigm across the firm, allowing researchers to work with datasets more friendly than raw PCAPs.
\item Led the design and implementation of Jump's USEQ ISO trading framework.
\end{tightemize}
